WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:01.810
(bright music)

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:03.230
- [Narrator] This ancient city was once

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.800
the cosmopolitan center
for the Kingdom of Pagan.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.633
The first Kingdom to unify the
regions that created Burma.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.640
The Bagan archeological zone

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.090
is an ancient city located
in Central Myanmar.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.350
It is known for being covered
in incredibly ornate temples,

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.820
which stand out of the
sweeping green plains

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.163
and lush vegetation.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.650
These temples were built
by the King's of Bagan

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.070
between 1057 and 1287.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.760
There were originally around 10,000.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.880
However, today, just over 2,000 remain

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.140
in varying states of repair.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.020
The others have been lost
due to Mongol invasions

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.453
and, in more recent times, earthquakes.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.320
The remaining temples are maintained

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.800
and are constantly undergoing restorations

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.713
to keep them intact for
future generations to enjoy.

00:01:01.741 --> 00:01:04.324
(bright music)

